         "Bright orange dichromate (two Cr at +6) accepts 6 electrons in acidic solution to form two emerald-green Cr³⁺ ions (+3), oxidizing 6 pale-green Fe²⁺ ions to Fe³⁺ (E°_cell = +1.33 − 0.77 = +0.56 V). Because primary-standard K₂Cr₂O₇ is stable indefinitely and does not oxidize Cl⁻ in cold dilute HCl, this is the classic volumetric assay for iron ore.",
         ["K2Cr2O7", "FeSO4", "H2SO4", "Cr3+", "H2O"], "redox_titration",
