         r"k = A e^{-E_a / (RT)}",
         "Svante Arrhenius (1889) showed that rate constants increase exponentially with temperature because a molecule must possess kinetic energy ≥ activation energy E_a (the potential-energy barrier to the transition state) AND collide with proper steric orientation (captured in the pre-exponential frequency factor A). Catalysts speed up reactions by providing an alternative mechanism with a lower E_a.",
