         "Unifies thermodynamics and electrochemistry: the maximum electrical work obtainable from a reversible cell at constant T and P equals −ΔG° = nFE°_cell, where n is the moles of electrons transferred in the balanced redox equation and F = 96,485 C/mol e⁻ is Faraday's constant (1 V = 1 J/C). Thus E°_cell > 0 guarantees ΔG° < 0 and K > 1.",
